# Dependent-origination core spine v1.30

The parent definition remains contextual composable transport.

Version 1.30 upgrades the v1.29 one-way scaled-horn transport to a
presentation-independent fibrancy statement:

```text
scaled horn family HX
  <-> scaled horn family HY
      via bidirectional horn-presentation equivalence

HasScaledHornFillers HX
  <-> HasScaledHornFillers HY
```

This is deliberately weaker than claiming the two ambient scaled simplicial
sets are literally equal or already equivalent as complete global `(∞,2)`
models.  It isolates exactly the structure needed for horn-filler invariance.

Consequently the higher-coherence invariant now has three layers:

1. intrinsic 1/2-cell invariance;
2. normalization-choice invariance;
3. scaled-horn fibrancy invariance under horn-presentation equivalence.

The next frontier is to construct such horn-presentation equivalences from
suitably normalized bicategorical model equivalences and then compare complete
scaled global models.
-/

